	(footprint "Connector_USB_Custom:USB_C_Receptacle_HRO_TYPE-C-31-D-09"
		(layer "B.Cu")
		(uuid "df747aea-59cd-4f7c-838c-88ed63805f08")
		(at 159 137)
		(descr "HRO (Korean Hroparts Elec) TYPE-C-31-D-09, LCSC C7463258 -- vertical-mount, through-hole USB-C 16P receptacle (USB 2.0 pinout, no SS/TX/RX). Hand-authored: no stock KiCad footprint exists for this exact manufacturer part (same situation as the RP2350B QFN-80 and the FPC connector on this project -- see Connector_FPC.pretty). Selected and dimensioned in .research/findings/2026-11-15-vertical-usb-c-receptacle-selection.md (pilink-0do); this footprint implements that finding's geometry for pilink-7el.11. Datasheet (fetched and read directly, krhro.com via LCSC, 2026-11-15): https://datasheet.lcsc.com/datasheet/pdf/26cf9302eb505927cdbd9bd7e2981be6.pdf?productCode=C7463258 -- confirmed directly against this footprint: 16 round signal PTHs at 0.70mm drill / 0.90mm pad on 1.10mm pitch, 7.70mm total column span (both datasheet-labeled, matches the research finding exactly); 4 oval shell/peg plated slots, 0.60x1.30mm drill in 1.00x1.70mm pad (datasheet-labeled, matches finding exactly), 4.30mm pitch between the top and bottom slot rows (datasheet-labeled, matches finding exactly); 6.50mm body height above the PCB and 2.10mm leg length (both datasheet-labeled, matches finding exactly); 8.34x2.56mm connector opening (datasheet-labeled -- this is the mating-face opening, not the shell outline, per the finding's correction). Two dimensions used below are NOT explicitly called out as distinct values anywhere in the research finding and were read directly off this footprint's own 'RECOMMENDED P.C.B. LAYOUT' view: the 1.35mm full center-to-center Y spacing between the A-row and B-row of signal pads (so each row sits +-0.675mm off the footprint's Y centerline) -- confirmed correct by independent re-measurement during PR #41 review (2026-11-15) -- and the X offset of the 4 shell/peg slots from centerline. The slot X offset was originally mis-measured as ~3.30mm; corrected here to +-2.50mm after PR #41's NOT-APPROVED review and a second, careful read of the datasheet's own PCB-layout-recommendation drawing. That drawing's nested dimension lines read, outer to inner: 7.70mm (full span between the outer A1/A12 signal pads), 5.50mm (full span between the A4/A9 signal pads), 5.00mm (full center-to-center spacing between the two shell/peg slots -- i.e. +-2.50mm off centerline), and 3.30mm (full span between the A5/A8 signal pads, 3x the 1.10mm pitch). The original ~3.30mm slot-offset figure was this same real datasheet dimension misapplied to the wrong feature (a signal-pad span, not a slot offset); as drawn, each mounting peg would have sat 0.8mm outboard of its physical slot and the part could not have been inserted. Both the row-Y-spacing and slot-X-offset figures are now independently confirmed against the datasheet drawing itself; no further human cross-check is flagged for either. The S1 pads' erroneous 'pad_prop_heatsink' property (a copy-paste artifact with no basis for a mechanical/shield pad) was also removed in this fix. Body/courtyard outline approximates the shell's outer envelope (~9.0 x 3.2mm) and the finding's recommended back-side courtyard (~9.0 x 5.3mm, since the slot/peg pads exceed the shell body on the short axis) -- not independently re-measured pixel-for-pixel here, reusing the finding's own figures per task instruction. The F.SilkS outline's short-axis edges were additionally pulled in from +-1.6mm to +-1.4mm (vs. the F.Fab outline, which stays at +-1.6mm to document the actual body envelope) specifically to clear the slot/peg pads (Y +-2.15mm, 1.0mm pad height -> inner edge at 1.65mm) and avoid a silk-over-copper DRC flag; this is a silkscreen/documentation-layer adjustment only and does not change the modeled body dimension. This is a back-side-mounted (PCB back) through-hole part per the upright-desk-clock form-factor decision; authored here as a normal front-side footprint, as KiCad auto-mirrors layers when placed on the back -- actual back-side placement is pilink-7el.12's job, out of scope here. Mounting/retention: through-hole shell pegs (not SMT tabs), consistent with pilink-0do's selection rationale. No DRC/PCB placement performed by this bead (hardware/placeholder.kicad_pcb has no real board layout yet) -- full fit/clearance verification happens at PCB layout time (pilink-7el.12) with a human running kicad-cli pcb drc and a visual GUI pass.")
		(tags "usb usb-c 2.0 vertical through-hole HRO")
